# ============================================================
# orbit: leo_dawn_dusk -- sun-synchronous, 550 km, along the terminator
# ============================================================
# The plane faces the Sun (beta near 90 degrees), so the satellite is in
# sunlight the whole orbit: the hot case. Around the June solstice the Sun
# leaves the plane's normal far enough for short eclipses (about 20 minutes). Open it in the GUI's Plans tab to see
# it propagated on the wall clock (docs/ORBIT.md).
#
# J2 turns the plane with the Sun, about a degree a day, so it keeps its local
# time all year.

epoch 2026-10-05T12:00:00Z
a 6928 km
e 0.001
i 97.6 deg
raan 281.3 deg
argp 0 deg
nu 0 deg
